            <div xml:id="d897">

                <pb facs="1006" n="862" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg862"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11N15/302: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-03-11T19:00:00+08:00">March 11, 1929—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 11—1:50 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>168. Your 79, February 27, midnight, which was repeated to Shanghai for Spiker
                    and to Nanking for me.</p>
                <pb facs="1007" n="863" xml:id="pg863"/>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>On March 7th, at Nanking, I pointed out to the Minister, and he agreed,
                        that the Woo claims and the question of interest, being matters beyond the
                        scope of the Commission, should be reserved for subsequent diplomatic
                        negotiations between the two Governments.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Without being precise as to date or amount, I urged Wang to cause payment
                        of further installments to be hastened. He stated that he would consult with
                        the Minister of Finance with that end in view.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
